module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.call_expression_erased_at_v2_body_lowering

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data call_expression_erased_at_v2_body_lowering: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "call_expression_erased_at_v2_body_lowering" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a call expression is erased by v2 normalize before resolve runs, so every reference it carries -- callee and arguments -- is invisible to name resolution and the refusal a missing declaration should raise has nothing to fire on** (INVALID STATE: v2.compiler.normalize, via v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold, lowers a function body that is a call into a Transform node whose only child is the `dag_token_lbrace` atom. The callee identity and every argument subtree are dropped. The module then passes normalize and resolve Accepted, with no diagnostic of any severity).",

    "HARM. v2 name resolution failed OPEN for the whole call-expression population while lowering dropped the call: a name no declaration provides was Accepted. The namespace cut's census rests on a delete-first premise, that removing an authority makes every real dependent REFUSE LOUDLY, and that premise is void for every dependent reached through an erased call. Native census mode still performs no resolution and cannot establish binding-refusal completeness. A native run with no passing call-bearing identities does not by itself identify lowering as the cause of every refused identity.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS, because two neighbouring rows look like this one and are not. `unresolved_callee_conflated_with_dispatched_elsewhere` is the v1 ExprCall-tail class: there the callee reaches the classifier and the miss is absorbed later. AT FILING (2026-09-12 interpreter dumps), the v2 callee never reached resolve at all: the earlier dated measurements (v2.test.claim.dag_acceptance frontier_arm_note, and a since-deleted staged_front_end commentary row) attributed the silence to resolve, which was the wrong stage — resolve is correct over the tree it receives, and that tree had already lost the call, so a resolve-side wall would have been a decoration because the undeclared-callee RED and the declared-callee positive control arrived as identical trees. THIS HEAD DOES NOT ENROLL A DISCRIMINATING RED for those two trees (review 66256): the cost-debt identities that could have carried undefined_callee_zzz / step-arity were left unedited so they would not face the post-#11195 100ms-equivalent eval-step budget. Native remains unshown.",

    "RECEIPT (2026-09-12, still-eagle-447, NAMESPACE XL-2 scoping). The normalized tree was dumped for five bodies via prepare_grammar, parse_module_prepared and normalize -- the calls v2.compiler.program_assembly program_assembly_read_to_normalized_root_prepared makes, and so the census route's own hand-off (v2.compiler.compile native_test_context_from_ingest). `{ k }` keeps `Atom:k`. `{ x }` over a parameter keeps `Atom:x`. `{ g(x: 1) }` with g declared, `{ zzz(x: 1) }` and `{ zzz(1) }` with zzz undeclared all become `Transform [ Atom:dag_token_lbrace ]`. The unprepared parse_module route (v2.compiler.staged_front_end run_front_end) dumps identically, so this is not a second lossy route beside a faithful one.",

    "EVIDENCE LEVEL, stated so the receipt is not read one rung high. The dumps ran the v2 .dag through the gunbc interpreter at main f9d37e43a1, and a structural node-count fold (not a printer) agrees: the parse tree grows with a call's arguments and nesting, while the normalized body of { g(x: 1) } is exactly one node larger than { k } -- the Transform and its lbrace atom -- and { g(x: h(y: 5)) } is no larger than that. A second named argument adds one node, so the lowering keeps something per extra argument, but none of the callee or argument content. That the natively emitted normalize behaves identically is not executed. The native route gives no contrary evidence: its receipt on the #10940 head (eager-raven-113, 2026-09-12) holds exactly one Passed identity, a literal-bodied smoke test, and every richer body refuses before or at eval (v2.compiler.infer node_grounding_frontier_note). So no route has been observed to lower a call faithfully.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: the minimum across in-scope paths (DESIGN section 4b). Interpreter prepared and unprepared: unshown on this head — no enrolled witness goes red if erasure is restored (body_lowering_normalize_accepts_projection_module and body_lowering_projection_lowers_to_transform were green under Transform[Atom:dag_token_lbrace]). Native realization of a declared argument-dependent call is not executed here. The class rung is therefore outside the ladder on every in-scope path until an enrolled discriminating control lands.",

    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed. Whether a name is bound in the containment index is decidable, and v2 resolve already refuses an unbound VALUE name with `resolve_reason_unbound_symbol`. The missing piece is not an authority but the lowering preserving what resolve needs.",

    "PARTIAL CLIMB (2026-09-14, #11322). The compiler threads Outcome through infix/call/arg lowering and applies calls as Transform with callee at position 0. That is not a rung: no enrolled identity distinguishes preserved callee/arguments from erasure. Extra predicates were not placed on staged_front_end_unbound_value_name_refuses_with_its_own_reason or body_lowering_normalize_accepts_projection_module (floor_cost_debt; editing them selects the post-#11195 100ms-equivalent eval-step budget against ~500k / ~1M measured work). Dedicated filing test fns were enrolment-censored at the 500ms ceiling (b561123). Arm (i) is not delivered.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, naming the residual capability: an enrolled interpreter control that REDs when callee or arguments are dropped (plus a positive control), AND a call with a DECLARED callee executes through the NATIVE route and returns the expected ARGUMENT-DEPENDENT result. A compiler comment, an RFM sentence, or a normalize-Accepted identity does not fire this trigger.",

    "CENSUS CONSEQUENCE, recorded because the cut consumes it: the whole-tree native census (the emitted closure binary's census mode) runs only tokenize, parse and normalize per file and never calls resolve, so its roster carries front-end refusals only. Restoring call lowering does not by itself add resolve refusals to that census. That needs the census mode to resolve per module as well.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
